  "_id": "fhSubStellarMist",
  "name": "Stellar Mist",
  "type": "consumable",
  "img": "icons/svg/item-bag.svg",
  "folder": "fhSubSciFi000001",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>A pearlescent suspension that dissolves in air. The user experiences sensations from elsewhere (sometimes elsewhen) for the duration. Operators learn not to trust the visions, but everyone tries them once. Sealed in a pressurized canister, it can be thrown to burst into a glittering cloud.</p><p><strong><em>Desired effects on use.</em></strong> For 1 hour you have advantage on Intelligence (Investigation) checks, disadvantage on Wisdom saving throws, and a +1d4 bonus to all saving throws.</p><p><strong><em>On use, save against addiction.</em></strong> Make a DC 15 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, you gain the Addicted condition from Stellar Mist (see below).</p><p><strong><em>Addicted from Stellar Mist.</em></strong> While you have this Addicted condition, you are also Poisoned and have disadvantage on Wisdom (Insight) and Wisdom (Perception) checks.</p><p><strong><em>Withdrawal.</em></strong> At the end of each Long Rest while addicted, you either take another dose or abstain. If you abstain, make a DC 13 Wisdom check to resist the craving; on a failure, you give in and take a dose. On a success, you go into withdrawal for 7 days, or half that if you succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw. If you have no doses left, skip the Wisdom check. While in withdrawal you have disadvantage on Wisdom and Intelligence saving throws, and in combat you take 1d4 psychic damage at the start of each of your turns. Abstaining then takes only the Wisdom check, and taking any dose ends the withdrawal but not the addiction. When the withdrawal ends, so does the addiction.</p><p><strong><em>Overdose.</em></strong> If you take a dose while still under its effects, or once your tolerance is at its limit, there is a 10% chance you overdose: you take 2d6 psychic damage and have the Incapacitated condition for 1 round.</p><p><strong><em>Dosing others.</em></strong> As an action, you can blow a dose into the face of a creature within 5 feet. It must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or be dosed. Or, as an action, you can throw a dose as a gas bomb at a point within 30 feet. It bursts into a 20-foot-radius cloud that lasts 1 minute. Each creature in the cloud other than you must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or be dosed. Any other creature that enters the cloud or starts its turn there must also make the saving throw, but no creature can be dosed by it more than once per turn.</p><p><em>Requires ready paraphernalia that applies to inhaled substances, such as a Vapor Mask or a Neural Diffuser.</em></p>"
    },
